{"format":1,"seq":355,"writes":[{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"delta","ops":[["p",["generation","message","content"],1,0,[{"type":"text","text":"pi-durable has no rendering hook today, but adding one is straightforward: the tool declares how its calls should be shown, and pi-action uses that when present. The pit-specific parsing then moves to pit. I haven't changed any code; this is a proposal.\n\n## What exists now\n\n- In pi-durable 1.5.2, a `ToolRegistration` has `execute`, `prepareArguments`, `outputLimits` and similar fields, but nothing for display. The tool-call types in pi-ai don't have any either.\n- pi's coding agent has `renderCall` and `renderResult`, but they return terminal UI components, so a CI log can't use them.\n- A result can carry `details`, which pi-durable describes as being \"for UIs\". Stored tool results keep it (`ToolResultMessage.details`). That only helps with the `↳` line, though: the `🔧` line is logged as soon as the model makes the call, before any result exists.\n- pi-action already holds the live tool objects of every pi-durable extension it loads (`src/durable-extensions.ts`), so it can call a function on a tool directly.\n\n## Proposal: an optional `present` field on the tool\n\nEach tool returns plain text, and the host decides how to lay it out (group, truncation, markers):\n\n```ts\ntype ToolPresentation<Args> = {\n\t/** When the call starts: one line, and optional details. */\n\tcall?(args: Args): { title: string; body?: string };\n\t/** When it ends: replaces \"N lines\" in the summary, and the arguments and output in the details. */\n\tresult?(args: Args, result: ToolResultMessage): { summary?: string; body?: string };\n};\n\n// On ToolRegistration:\nreadonly present?: ToolPresentation<ToolArgs<TParameters>>;\n```\n\nRules for hosts, so that rendering stays safe and the same every time:\n- **Pure and synchronous.** pi-action logs from stored entries, including after a replay. The functions should only use their inputs (`args`, and `result` with its `details`), not live state.\n- **Plain text.** No colours or widgets, so a TUI, a web UI and the workflow log can all use it.\n- **The host keeps control.** pi-action still cuts long lines, shows only the last 30 lines, and blocks `"}]],["a",["generation","message","content",0,"thinkingSignature"],""],["a",["generation","message","content",1,"text"],"::workflow-commands::`. If `present` throws or returns something invalid, it falls back to the generic rendering and logs a debug message.\n\npit's `typescript` tool would then return:\n- **`call`:** the label from `// @pit:`"]]}}]}